A guide for developing Old School RuneScape plugins for the RuneLite client, covering project structure, API integration, and publishing.

## Overview

RuneLite plugins extend the RuneLite client to add new features for OSRS players. This skill covers the complete workflow from scaffolding a plugin to publishing it to the plugin hub.

## Project Structure

```
plugin-name/
├── src/main/java/com/itmeansbigmountain/pluginname/
│   ├── PluginNamePlugin.java      # Main plugin class
│   ├── PluginNameConfig.java      # Configuration interface
│   └── PluginNameOverlay.java     # UI overlay (optional)
├── plugin.json                     # Plugin metadata
├── README.md                       # Documentation
└── build.gradle                    # Build configuration
```

## Plugin Development Patterns

### 1. Plugin Entry Point
```java
@Slf4j
@PluginDescriptor(
    name = "Plugin Name",
    description = "Brief description",
    tags = {"tag1", "tag2"}
)
public class PluginNamePlugin extends Plugin {
    @Inject private Client client;
    @Inject private PluginNameConfig config;

    @Override
    protected void startUp() { /* init */ }
    @Override
    protected void shutDown() { /* cleanup */ }
}
```

### 2. Configuration Interface
```java
@ConfigGroup("pluginname")
public interface PluginNameConfig extends Config {
    @ConfigItem("showOverlay", "Show Overlay")
    default boolean showOverlay() { return true; }
}
```

### 3. Event Handling
```java
@Subscribe
public void onChatMessage(ChatMessage event) {
    // Handle chat events
}

@Subscribe
public void onGameTick(GameTick event) {
    // Handle game ticks
}
```

### 4. External API Integration
- Use shared API clients (WOMApiClient, TempleApiClient)
- Implement proper error handling and fallbacks
- Cache responses to avoid rate limiting
- Use async HTTP calls where possible

## Common APIs

| API | Purpose | Rate Limits |
|-----|---------|-------------|
| WiseOldMan | XP tracking, competition data | 500 req/hour |
| TempleOSRS | Boss KC, competition data | 120 req/minute |
| RuneLite API | Game state, events | No limits |

## Best Practices

1. **Performance**: Avoid blocking the game thread; use background executors
